A||||5||fiero87||Help...is it the same???||||5||
Z||000000||fiero87||05-16-2001||03:07 AM||||Hello fourm members..<P>In my search for a new engine for my 86 GT i have found a 2.8 MPFI with 20,000 miles on it for only $250 dollars.  Its complete and was a crate motor from GM.  It was installed into an 86 Z-24 less than a year ago.  Is this the same engine as in the fiero?  Will everything bolt up/work properly?  Are the horsepower figures the same as the stock engine?  Any info would be greatly appreciated....Thanks<BR>Tim||||reg||5
Z||000001||mrfiero||05-16-2001||05:04 AM||||They are different.  FWD 2.8's (Cavalier, Beretta, etc.) use aluminum heads and aren't easily adapted for use in the Fiero (which uses cast iron heads).  The Fieros intake stuff doesn't bolt onto the aluminum heads plus the pistons are dished, so just swapping the heads isn't an option either.  Sorry.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Raydar||05-16-2001||09:53 AM||||If it was a crate motor for an 86, wouldn't it have the iron heads? GM didn't introduce the aluminum heads until later. <BR>If it has iron heads, it ought to be a bolt-in.  <P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<P>88 black Formula<BR>88 Duke coupe <BR>88 "wadded up" Formula (parts car)||||reg||5
Z||000003||ironhedno3||05-16-2001||10:41 AM||||raydar is correct..if it was for an 86 cavalier and not an 87 it is the exact same engine||||reg||6
Z||000004||fiero87||05-16-2001||11:23 AM||||Thats what i thought too.  I'm sure its the iron head version cause this is one old caviler.  The intake plenum is very plain, so i'm assuming i'm going to use the fiero intake, but otherwise everything else down should be the same i thought...  Thanks<BR>Tim||||reg||10
Z||000005||87GTZ34||05-16-2001||01:52 PM||||You may want to verify that the heads (although they're iron) have the larger valves.  If they don't, have your heads reworked and put them on the newer engine.  If you don't use the larger valves there will be a noticable difference in torque/power.  My 1st '87GT had the motor swapped just b4 I bought it with the lower perf version and it was a dog right up to the point that I turned a bearing.<p>[This message has been edited by 87GTZ34 (edited 05-16-2001).]||||reg||1
